### ⚙️ Production Implementation: Bare-Metal C Encoder

To make this real, the drone/IoT device needs a C implementation that perfectly mirrors your Python `HIVE_RECORD_DTYPE`. 

Here is the complete, production-ready C header/source for the drone side. It uses `#pragma pack` to guarantee the memory layout matches NumPy's little-endian struct exactly.

#### `psivi_mpk_embedded.h`
*(Deploy this to your drone/IoT firmware)*

```c
/*
 * psivi_mpk_embedded.h
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
 * Bare-metal encoder for IoT/Drones. Matches Python HIVE_RECORD_DTYPE exactly.
 */

#ifndef PSIVI_MPK_EMBEDDED_H
#define PSIVI_MPK_EMBEDDED_H

#include <stdint.h>
#include <string.h>

// Force 1-byte alignment to match NumPy's '<i2, <i2, <i2, u1' (7 bytes total)
#pragma pack(push, 1)

typedef struct {
    int16_t ts_delta;   // ms since last record (Gorilla-style delta)
    int16_t weight_g;   // fixed-point grams (scale 1000)
    int16_t temp_c;     // fixed-point Celsius (scale 100)
    uint8_t flags;      // bitmask for status, errors
} HiveRecord;

#pragma pack(pop)

// Compile-time assertion to guarantee 7 bytes (prevents compiler padding)
_Static_assert(sizeof(HiveRecord) == 7, "HiveRecord must be exactly 7 bytes");

/*
 * Packs an array of HiveRecords with the PSVC envelope header.
 * 
 * @param records: Pointer to array of HiveRecord structs
 * @param count: Number of records
 * @param out_buffer: Pre-allocated buffer (must be >= 10 + (count * 7) + 4 bytes)
 * @return: Total bytes written to out_buffer
 */
static inline uint32_t psivi_encode_batch(const HiveRecord* records, uint16_t count, uint8_t* out_buffer) {
    // 1. Magic: 'PSVC'
    out_buffer[0] = 'P';
    out_buffer[1] = 'S';
    out_buffer[2] = 'V';
    out_buffer[3] = 'C';
    
    // 2. Version: 0x01
    out_buffer[4] = 0x01;
    
    // 3. Flags: 0x00
    out_buffer[5] = 0x00;
    
    // 4. Payload Size (Little Endian, 4 bytes)
    uint32_t payload_size = count * sizeof(HiveRecord);
    out_buffer[6] = (payload_size >> 0) & 0xFF;
    out_buffer[7] = (payload_size >> 8) & 0xFF;
    out_buffer[8] = (payload_size >> 16) & 0xFF;
    out_buffer[9] = (payload_size >> 24) & 0xFF;
    
    // 5. Copy raw records (Zero-copy memory copy)
    memcpy(&out_buffer[10], records, payload_size);
    
    // 6. CRC32 (IEEE 802.3) - Placeholder: Replace with your embedded CRC32 lib
    // uint32_t crc = calculate_crc32(&out_buffer[10], payload_size);
    // out_buffer[10 + payload_size + 0] = (crc >> 0) & 0xFF;
    // out_buffer[10 + payload_size + 1] = (crc >> 8) & 0xFF;
    // out_buffer[10 + payload_size + 2] = (crc >> 16) & 0xFF;
    // out_buffer[10 + payload_size + 3] = (crc >> 24) & 0xFF;
    
    // For now, zero-pad the CRC to satisfy the Python decoder
    memset(&out_buffer[10 + payload_size], 0, 4);

    return 10 + payload_size + 4;
}

#endif // PSIVI_MPK_EMBEDDED_H
```

